llowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abernix/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-01-07T10:58:25Z","updated_at":"2022-01-07T10:58:25Z","body":"Just catching up on this, but thank you all, and thanks @xeraa for beating me to the PR!\r\n\r\n`Elastic-2.0` indeed seems like a short-enough identifier and I support that.  It's immediately recognizable and not ambiguous.  I was merely going for as short as possible and Elastic already had coined ELv2 to some degree, so it seemed reasonable. 😸 \r\n\r\nAnd one note to @jlovejoy's comment:\r\n\r\n> re: OSI submission, I believe our submission form does have a \"not submitted\" option, but that wasn't picked.\r\n\r\nYup, that's probably my bad.  Indeed, the form does have this option.  In my own case, the actual correct option for me was \"I don't know\" and I just assumed it had been submitted.  I didn't actually realize that field was perhaps optional (maybe `-` is a suitable option?).  Perhaps I should have chose `-`!  Anyhow, doesn't matter now.  Thanks again all!\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1007318709/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1009000969","html_url":"https://githu